WEBVTT

00:00:02.796 --> 00:00:03.797
Giulia!

00:00:03.881 --> 00:00:06.217
-Oh!
-(SPEAKING ITALIAN)

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:07.468
-Uh, grazie.
-Ciao.

00:00:07.551 --> 00:00:08.677
Hey, uh, Spewlia?

00:00:08.761 --> 00:00:10.888
Giulia. My name is Giulia.

00:00:11.347 --> 00:00:15.351
Okay. When you race in a cup,
what do you get?

00:00:16.101 --> 00:00:17.853
Soldi. Prize money.

00:00:18.187 --> 00:00:19.188
Oh.

00:00:19.271 --> 00:00:20.272
Okay.

00:00:20.356 --> 00:00:22.107
-No, no! Keep going!
-What? Why?

00:00:22.191 --> 00:00:23.192
Ask her about the prize money!

00:00:23.275 --> 00:00:24.318
But that stuff is useless.

00:00:24.401 --> 00:00:25.986
-Maybe that becomes a Vespa.
-How does that become...

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:27.279
-Just ask her!
-Fine, fine, fine.

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:29.490
-Hello again.
-Ciao.

00:00:29.573 --> 00:00:32.368
Can we turn the money into something else?

00:00:32.952 --> 00:00:34.703
-Something like...
-That.

00:00:35.871 --> 00:00:38.666
Pfft. No. But it could get you that.

00:00:40.584 --> 00:00:41.585
(GASPS)

00:00:41.669 --> 00:00:44.296
(SLOW ITALIAN POP MUSIC INTRO PLAYING)

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:45.756
(COINS JINGLING)

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:47.842
(MUSIC TEMPO INCREASES)

00:00:51.929 --> 00:00:53.013
BOTH: Whoo-hoo!

00:00:53.597 --> 00:00:54.598
It's so beautiful.

00:00:54.682 --> 00:00:56.016
Yes, we need it.

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:57.810
Great, so we'll just win the race.

00:00:57.893 --> 00:00:58.936
(BRAKES SQUEAL)

00:00:59.311 --> 00:01:00.521
You'll have to beat Ercole.

00:01:00.688 --> 00:01:02.064
Okay, so we'll beat Ercole.

00:01:02.147 --> 00:01:03.440
Huh. Really?

00:01:03.524 --> 00:01:05.484
Thinks he'll beat Ercole,
this guy. (CHUCKLES)

00:01:05.568 --> 00:01:07.194
First of all, get in line!

00:01:07.278 --> 00:01:10.781
Every summer, that jerk
makes my life miserable.

00:01:10.865 --> 00:01:13.701
So, no one's taking him down
unless it's me!

00:01:14.743 --> 00:01:16.787
Second, this isn't any old race.

00:01:16.954 --> 00:01:19.999
It's an epic, grueling,
traditional Italian triathlon.

00:01:20.082 --> 00:01:22.918
Swimming, cycling, and eating pasta.

00:01:23.169 --> 00:01:24.211
So, you'd need a teammate.

00:01:24.295 --> 00:01:26.964
Well, we'll figure it out.
Thanks, human girl.

00:01:28.632 --> 00:01:31.302
Hey, hey, wait. Wait, Alberto.

00:01:31.802 --> 00:01:33.137
What if we join her team?

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:34.263
GIULIA: Grazie! Arrivederci!

00:01:34.346 --> 00:01:35.973
Hmm. Better idea.

00:01:36.056 --> 00:01:37.558
Hey, Spew... Girl!

00:01:37.641 --> 00:01:38.726
Santa mozzarella.

00:01:38.809 --> 00:01:40.853
Congratulations, you're joining our team.

00:01:40.936 --> 00:01:42.813
(SCOFFS) I race alone.

00:01:43.480 --> 00:01:44.940
(GRUNTING)

00:01:45.024 --> 00:01:46.108
(ALL GRUNTING)

00:01:48.068 --> 00:01:50.446
But we could be under the dogs, too.

00:01:50.529 --> 00:01:51.739
Hey, it's okay, Luca.

00:01:51.822 --> 00:01:54.200
She'd rather do
the whole race alone again.

00:01:54.283 --> 00:01:55.951
Maybe this time
she won't throw up as much.

00:01:56.035 --> 00:01:57.453
Uh, hang on.

00:01:59.997 --> 00:02:01.957
You wanna be on my team, eh?

00:02:02.249 --> 00:02:03.501
Let's see what you got.

00:02:05.294 --> 00:02:06.337
(YELPS)

00:02:06.879 --> 00:02:09.131
-(WHISPERING INDISTINCTLY)
-(CHUCKLES SHEEPISHLY)

00:02:09.215 --> 00:02:10.341
All right, try jumping onto it.

00:02:11.342 --> 00:02:12.343
-(GRUNTS)
-No, no, no.

00:02:12.426 --> 00:02:14.053
You gotta show it you're the boss!

00:02:14.595 --> 00:02:15.846
(WHIMPERS)

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:17.473
(SIGHS) Santa mozzarella.

00:02:17.556 --> 00:02:18.849
-Eyes up.
-LUCA: Huh?

00:02:18.933 --> 00:02:21.101
Looking down is what's making you fall.

00:02:24.021 --> 00:02:25.022
LUCA: Whoa.

00:02:25.105 --> 00:02:26.524
-(LUCA WHIMPERS)
-(LADY SPEAKS ITALIAN)

00:02:27.274 --> 00:02:28.651
Whoa. I'm doing it.

00:02:30.027 --> 00:02:31.403
So, can we be on the team?

00:02:31.487 --> 00:02:32.738
(REPLIES IN ITALIAN)

00:02:32.822 --> 00:02:33.906
Can you dodge obstacles?

00:02:33.989 --> 00:02:35.908
What if an old lady crosses your path?

00:02:35.991 --> 00:02:37.243
-(YELLING)
-(LUCA GASPS)

00:02:37.326 --> 00:02:39.912
Can you withstand
passive-aggressive verbal assaults?

00:02:39.995 --> 00:02:41.956
(IMITATES ERCOLE) "Nice bike,
Number One and Number Two.

00:02:42.039 --> 00:02:43.040
"I was kidding.

00:02:43.123 --> 00:02:44.583
"Your bike is a disgrace." (LAUGHS)

00:02:44.959 --> 00:02:46.043
Finally, can you handle

00:02:46.126 --> 00:02:48.337
the course's fiendishly difficult terrain?

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:49.797
Silenzio, Bruno.

00:02:54.385 --> 00:02:56.262
(WHIMPERS AND YELPS)

00:02:57.096 --> 00:02:58.097
Hmm.

00:03:00.349 --> 00:03:01.767
Stop. What about you?

00:03:01.851 --> 00:03:02.935
Can you swim at least?

00:03:03.018 --> 00:03:06.856
Yeah, I'm amazingly (GRUNTS)
bad at swimming.

00:03:06.939 --> 00:03:09.316
You can't swim,
you can barely ride a bike.

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:10.776
(EXCLAIMS IN ITALIAN)

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:12.653
I mean, where are you even from?

00:03:12.736 --> 00:03:14.155
We're not telling you our secrets!

00:03:14.238 --> 00:03:16.031
-We're runaways.
-Runaways?

00:03:16.115 --> 00:03:17.449
I don't know, ragazzi...

00:03:18.117 --> 00:03:19.118
Please?

00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:21.912
My family was gonna send me
somewhere horrible.

00:03:21.996 --> 00:03:23.831
Away from everything I love.

00:03:23.998 --> 00:03:26.375
But if we win this race, well,

00:03:26.458 --> 00:03:27.835
we can be free.

00:03:28.919 --> 00:03:30.963
My life's great. I'm just helping him out.

00:03:31.046 --> 00:03:32.173
Hmm.

00:03:32.256 --> 00:03:33.716
Just give me one more chance.

00:03:34.216 --> 00:03:35.217
No.

00:03:35.843 --> 00:03:37.553
You guys want it just as bad as I do.

00:03:37.636 --> 00:03:38.637
You have the hunger.

00:03:38.721 --> 00:03:39.930
That's the most important thing.

00:03:40.097 --> 00:03:41.432
I'm definitely hungry.

00:03:41.515 --> 00:03:44.310
Perfetto! You eat, you bike, and I swim.

00:03:44.393 --> 00:03:46.687
-(BOTH LAUGH)
-GIULIA: Underdogs?

00:03:47.646 --> 00:03:48.939
ALBERTO AND LUCA: Underdogs.

00:03:49.356 --> 00:03:51.609
Now we just need money for the entry fee.

00:03:51.775 --> 00:03:53.277
From my dad.

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:54.862
(OPERATIC MUSIC PLAYING OVER RADIO)

00:03:54.945 --> 00:03:56.655
(MAN SINGING ALONG IN ITALIAN)

00:03:56.739 --> 00:03:58.282
(VOCALIZES ALONG TO MUSIC)

00:03:58.365 --> 00:04:00.367
(SINGING ALONG TO ARIA)

00:04:02.536 --> 00:04:05.623
All right, just let me do the talking
and act casual.

00:04:05.706 --> 00:04:07.166
He doesn't do well with fear.

00:04:07.249 --> 00:04:08.709
Hey, Papà! I brought

00:04:08.792 --> 00:04:10.169
-some friends for dinner.
-(BOTH GASP)

00:04:10.252 --> 00:04:11.837
-Is there enough for four?
-(KNIFE CHOPS)

00:04:12.922 --> 00:04:14.548
(OPERATIC MUSIC CONTINUES OVER RADIO)

00:04:14.632 --> 00:04:15.799
-(WHIMPERS)
-Whoa.

00:04:15.883 --> 00:04:17.635
What's wrong with you, stu...
(GRUNTS)

00:04:17.718 --> 00:04:18.719
(CHUCKLES SHEEPISHLY)

00:04:19.136 --> 00:04:20.137
(GRUNTS)

00:04:25.309 --> 00:04:26.894
What do you think he kills with those?

00:04:27.853 --> 00:04:30.231
-MASSIMO: Anything that swims.
-(CHUCKLES NERVOUSLY)

00:04:30.314 --> 00:04:32.024
Hai visto il giornale today?

00:04:32.107 --> 00:04:34.151
(SIGHS) That photo is a fake, Papà.

00:04:34.818 --> 00:04:38.072
Everyone in Portorosso
pretends to believe in sea monsters.

00:04:38.572 --> 00:04:40.491
-(LUCA GASPS)
-ALBERTO: Huh.

00:04:40.574 --> 00:04:42.660
MASSIMO: Well, I'm not pretending.

00:04:44.662 --> 00:04:45.871
-(LUCA GASPS)
-Huh? (YELLS)

00:04:49.542 --> 00:04:50.751
(CAT GRUMBLES)

00:04:53.337 --> 00:04:54.338
(LAUGHS SHEEPISHLY)

00:04:56.340 --> 00:04:57.675
Slipped.

00:04:59.426 --> 00:05:00.427
Eh.

00:05:01.846 --> 00:05:02.888
BOTH: Phew!

00:05:02.972 --> 00:05:04.682
(CAT GROWLING)

00:05:05.808 --> 00:05:06.934
MASSIMO: Dinner's ready.

00:05:07.351 --> 00:05:08.978
Trenette al pesto.

00:05:09.478 --> 00:05:11.272
(OPERATIC MUSIC CONTINUES OVER RADIO)

00:05:11.355 --> 00:05:12.356
(SPEAKS ITALIAN)

00:05:12.439 --> 00:05:13.691
(HOUSE RATTLES)

00:05:19.864 --> 00:05:20.865
(LAUGHS SHEEPISHLY)

00:05:22.616 --> 00:05:23.701
(GULPS)

00:05:31.041 --> 00:05:32.084
(GASPS)

00:05:32.168 --> 00:05:33.252
Mmm!

00:05:33.335 --> 00:05:35.087
(CHOMPING AND GRUNTING)

00:05:37.214 --> 00:05:38.215
Uh...

00:05:38.883 --> 00:05:39.884
LUCA: Mmm!

00:05:41.343 --> 00:05:42.344
Okay.

00:05:43.679 --> 00:05:46.140
Where did you boys say you were from?

00:05:46.223 --> 00:05:47.933
(CAT GRUMBLES)

00:05:48.017 --> 00:05:50.561
(NERVOUSLY) They're, uh,
classmates. From Genova.

00:05:50.644 --> 00:05:52.354
Luca and, uh...

00:05:52.438 --> 00:05:54.273
-(SOFTLY) Alberto.
-Alberto.

00:05:54.982 --> 00:05:57.484
And what brings you to Portorosso?

00:05:57.568 --> 00:05:58.652
GIULIA: Oh. Uh...

00:05:58.736 --> 00:06:00.029
Funny you should ask.

00:06:00.112 --> 00:06:01.322
They came for the race.

00:06:01.989 --> 00:06:03.073
The race?

00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:04.450
Yeah.

00:06:04.533 --> 00:06:07.161
Uh, you know what? Don't worry about it.

00:06:07.244 --> 00:06:09.121
(SCOFFS) "Don't worry about it"?

00:06:09.497 --> 00:06:11.499
Mm-hmm. Don't worry about it.

00:06:11.582 --> 00:06:14.752
MASSIMO: (SIGHS) Giulietta. A word.

00:06:16.545 --> 00:06:18.464
I don't want you doing the race again.

00:06:18.547 --> 00:06:19.715
You get so upset.

00:06:19.798 --> 00:06:22.259
Papà, per favore, I have a team now.

00:06:22.343 --> 00:06:25.346
There's also the entry fee.
Money is tight.

00:06:25.429 --> 00:06:27.556
I'll work double shifts at the pescheria.
Whatever you need.

00:06:27.640 --> 00:06:29.975
I can't sell what I don't have.

00:06:30.059 --> 00:06:32.394
What I need is more fish in my net.

00:06:32.978 --> 00:06:34.688
(APOLOGIZES IN ITALIAN)

00:06:34.772 --> 00:06:36.398
LUCA: Um, excuse me?

00:06:36.482 --> 00:06:37.858
We could help.

00:06:37.942 --> 00:06:39.360
You know fish?

00:06:39.443 --> 00:06:41.278
Oh, we? We know lots of fish.

00:06:41.362 --> 00:06:43.531
-MASSIMO: Huh.
-Can this face lose?

00:06:43.614 --> 00:06:44.907
(SIGHS HEAVILY)

00:06:45.407 --> 00:06:48.244
You want to work? I'll put you to work.

00:06:48.327 --> 00:06:49.829
Really? (LAUGHING)

00:06:49.912 --> 00:06:51.622
(LAUGHING) Oh, grazie, Papà.

00:06:51.705 --> 00:06:53.457
-(CAT GROWLING)
-(LUCA WHIMPERS)

00:06:53.541 --> 00:06:54.792
(GROWLING)

00:06:54.875 --> 00:06:57.127
Machiavelli! (SHUSHES) Don't you...

00:06:57.211 --> 00:06:59.630
-No! Machiavelli!
-(LUCA SCREAMING)

00:07:00.881 --> 00:07:01.966
(LUCA PANTING)

00:07:02.049 --> 00:07:03.759
I'm so sorry about the cat.

00:07:03.843 --> 00:07:05.344
I don't know what got into him.

00:07:05.427 --> 00:07:08.305
It's fine. We're gonna head back to, uh...

00:07:08.848 --> 00:07:09.849
Oh!

00:07:09.932 --> 00:07:12.560
Do you guys need a place to stay?

00:07:14.186 --> 00:07:15.229
Cool.

00:07:15.396 --> 00:07:17.815
Oops! Sorry. This is my...

00:07:17.898 --> 00:07:18.899
Your hideout.

00:07:19.316 --> 00:07:21.652
Huh. Yeah. My hideout.

00:07:21.819 --> 00:07:23.737
Buonanotte, boys. (GRUNTS)

00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:25.281
Whoa!

00:07:25.364 --> 00:07:26.490
-(CRASHES)
-(MACHIAVELLI YOWLS)

00:07:26.574 --> 00:07:29.285
(CHUCKLES SHEEPISHLY) Slipped.
Uh, see you in the morning.

00:07:31.328 --> 00:07:32.830
-(SIGHS) That was close.
-I know.

00:07:32.913 --> 00:07:34.748
Like, how big was that dad human?

00:07:34.832 --> 00:07:36.333
That guy kills things, for sure.

00:07:36.417 --> 00:07:38.252
I thought we were gonna die,
like, a hundred times.

00:07:38.335 --> 00:07:39.336
Hey, relax.

00:07:39.420 --> 00:07:41.172
We're incredible at this humaning stuff.

00:07:41.255 --> 00:07:43.132
Yeah. You're right.

00:07:43.215 --> 00:07:44.550
Did you see me on the bike?

00:07:44.633 --> 00:07:45.759
Giulia said, "Look up,"

00:07:45.843 --> 00:07:47.178
and then all of a sudden, I was riding it.

00:07:47.261 --> 00:07:48.721
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
Our Vespa's gonna be

00:07:48.804 --> 00:07:50.556
even better than a bike, though.

00:07:50.639 --> 00:07:53.017
Because the moment we get it,
we're outta here.

00:07:53.434 --> 00:07:54.435
(CHUCKLES)

00:07:55.019 --> 00:07:57.646
I can't wait. (SIGHS DEEPLY)

